<change>
<description>Update the preview component with proper mock data for each banner</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { BannerContainer } from '../../../../packages/features/shell/banners/LayoutBanner';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    teamUpgradeBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Team Upgrade Banner',
    },
    orgUpgradeBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Org Upgrade Banner',
    },
    verifyEmailBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Verify Email Banner',
    },
    adminPasswordBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Admin Password Banner',
    },
    impersonationBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Impersonation Banner',
    },
    calendarCredentialBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Calendar Credential Banner',
    },
    invalidAppCredentialBanners: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Invalid App Credential Banners',
    },
  });

  // Mock data for each banner type
  const mockBanners = {
    teamUpgradeBanner: state.teamUpgradeBanner.value ? {
      data: {
        teams: [{ name: "Test Team" }],
        username: "testuser"
      }
    } : null,
    orgUpgradeBanner: state.orgUpgradeBanner.value ? {
      data: {
        organizations: [{ name: "Test Org" }],
        username: "testuser"
      }
    } : null,
    verifyEmailBanner: state.verifyEmailBanner.value ? {
      data: {
        email: "test@example.com",
        isVerified: false
      }
    } : null,
    adminPasswordBanner: state.adminPasswordBanner.value ? {
      data: {
        role: "ADMIN",
        usedSettingsPage: false
      }
    } : null,
    impersonationBanner: state.impersonationBanner.value ? {
      data: {
        impersonatedBy: {
          username: "admin"
        }
      }
    } : null,
    calendarCredentialBanner: state.calendarCredentialBanner.value ? {
      data: {
        hasCalendarIntegrations: false,
        hasBookings: true
      }
    } : null,
    invalidAppCredentialBanners: state.invalidAppCredentialBanners.value ? {
      data: [{
        appName: "Test App",
        appType: "calendar",
        title: "Invalid Credentials",
        message: "Please reconnect your calendar"
      }]
    } : null
  };

  return <BannerContainer banners={mockBanners} />;
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made the following changes to fix the errors:

1. For the "data.map is not a function" error in InvalidAppCredentialBanners:
   - Added proper mock data structure with an array containing a sample invalid credential

2. For the "data is not iterable" errors in TeamsUpgradeBanner and OrgUpgradeBanner:
   - Added mock data with arrays for teams and organizations

3. For the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'role')" error in AdminPasswordBanner:
   - Added mock data with role property

4. For the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'impersonatedBy')" error:
   - Added mock data with impersonatedBy property

5. For all banners:
   - Provided proper data structure matching what each banner component expects
   - Added null checks to prevent rendering when the banner is disabled
   - Used the state values to conditionally show/hide banners

This should resolve all the type errors and provide proper mock data for the banner components to render correctly. Each banner now has the minimum required data structure it expects to function properly.

