<description>Update the mock data structure to match what the banner components expect</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { BannerContainer } from '../../../../packages/features/shell/banners/LayoutBanner';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    teamUpgradeBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Team Upgrade Banner',
    },
    orgUpgradeBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Org Upgrade Banner',
    },
    verifyEmailBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Verify Email Banner',
    },
    adminPasswordBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Admin Password Banner',
    },
    impersonationBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Impersonation Banner',
    },
    calendarCredentialBanner: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Calendar Credential Banner',
    },
    invalidAppCredentialBanners: {
      type: 'boolean',
      value: true,
      label: 'Show Invalid App Credential Banners',
    },
  });

  // Mock data for each banner type
  const mockBanners = {
    teamUpgradeBanner: state.teamUpgradeBanner.value ? {
      teams: [{ 
        name: "Test Team",
        slug: "test-team",
        membership: { role: "MEMBER" }
      }]
    } : null,
    orgUpgradeBanner: state.orgUpgradeBanner.value ? {
      organizations: [{ 
        name: "Test Org",
        slug: "test-org",
        membership: { role: "MEMBER" }
      }]
    } : null,
    verifyEmailBanner: state.verifyEmailBanner.value ? {
      email: "test@example.com",
      isVerified: false
    } : null,
    adminPasswordBanner: state.adminPasswordBanner.value ? {
      user: {
        role: "ADMIN",
        username: "admin"
      },
      usedSettingsPage: false
    } : null,
    impersonationBanner: state.impersonationBanner.value ? {
      user: {
        impersonatedBy: {
          username: "admin",
          name: "Administrator"
        }
      }
    } : null,
    calendarCredentialBanner: state.calendarCredentialBanner.value ? {
      user: {
        hasCalendarIntegrations: false,
        hasBookings: true
      }
    } : null,
    invalidAppCredentialBanners: state.invalidAppCredentialBanners.value ? 
      [
        {
          appName: "Test App",
          appType: "calendar",
          title: "Invalid Credentials",
          message: "Please reconnect your calendar",
          integration: {
            name: "Test Integration",
            type: "calendar"
          }
        }
      ] : 
      []
  };

  // Only render banners that have data
  const filteredBanners = Object.fromEntries(
    Object.entries(mockBanners).filter(([_, value]) => value !== null)
  );

  try {
    return <BannerContainer banners={filteredBanners} />;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error rendering BannerContainer:', error);
    return null;
  }
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

Key changes made:

1. For `teamUpgradeBanner` and `orgUpgradeBanner`:
   - Added proper structure with membership information
   - Wrapped teams/organizations in an object instead of passing array directly

2. For `adminPasswordBanner`:
   - Added user object containing role and username
   - Wrapped properties in correct structure

3. For `impersonationBanner`:
   - Added user object containing impersonatedBy information
   - Added more complete impersonatedBy data

4. For `calendarCredentialBanner`:
   - Wrapped properties in user object

5. For `invalidAppCredentialBanners`:
   - Added more complete integration information
   - Ensured array structure is maintained

6. Added filtering to remove null values from banners object

These changes should resolve the property access errors by providing the correct data structure that each banner component expects. The data is now properly nested within the expected objects and contains all required properties.

